WEBVTT

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:06.110
That day, gasping for breath,

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:08.070
I sought my father.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:11.820
I felt certain that he
awaited me in this city.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:12.950
Father!

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.410
Edward.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:16.620
Anne.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.660
Pardon my delay.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.080
We've been waiting for you.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.790
So have the people of York.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.460
Waiting for Richard III to come home.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.720
Be a king for the sake of his name,
until you die in glory.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.720
York of the white rose.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.350
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:49.820
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:54.450
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:34.340
Rebellion?

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:38.970
I was astonished to hear it
from the Duke of Buckingham.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:44.890
He grew dissatisfied because the king
denied him his promised reward.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:46.680
In the end,

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:52.230
he came to worry that his own
head would be the next to roll.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:56.980
And so, he desires your aid. You are an
honorable gentleman and our comrade.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:00.990
Our rebellion needs
a trustworthy new leader.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.740
It's difficult to believe,

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:10.370
but if Buckingham, a great lord
and the king's right hand, revolts,

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:14.290
the foundations of Richard III's
reign will be worse than shaken.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.800
A rebel leader?

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.720
You called, Dad?

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.050
I've told you not to call--

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:28.180
Why, this is a once-in-a-lifetime
opportunity to get ahead!

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:33.650
If you play your cards right, you'll come
out on top no matter who triumphs!

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:39.360
But can you trust Buckingham?
He was so devoted to the king.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.360
Is that what you're thinking, Dad?

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.700
I concur.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.410
I have no wish to fight a losing battle.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.870
Then how about this?

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:54.040
Tell Buckingham to bring you a gift if
he's serious about turning on Richard.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.840
Those boys in the Tower are still alive.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:05.800
Many still view them as
the rightful heirs to the crown.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:06.640
I suppose.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:08.430
You <i>suppose</i>?!

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:11.390
You pose as a fence-sitter
in perfect safety,

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:16.270
all the while plotting to put your
stepson at the head of a rebel army!

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:19.070
I wish to be <i>king</i>, Father.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:22.360
And should a parent not
reward his child's efforts?

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:23.280
Hm?

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:27.570
Tell Buckingham that

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:32.540
you'll join forces with him if he
kills the children in the Tower.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.170
Damn Stanley.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:40.340
I anticipated this response,
but he's still a nuisance.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:45.470
But by joining forces with his stepson,
the Earl of Richmond,

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:49.220
I can win Lancastrian
support for my cause.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:55.440
I had considered how to eliminate those
boys as a means to protect Richard,

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:59.020
but if I kill them now,
Richard must be the culprit.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:01.980
When shall I kill him?

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:05.780
The time is not yet ripe.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:09.410
To kill Richard,
we'll first need a sacrifice.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:12.370
Will that truly save him?

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.410
Yes, and you as well.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.330
Is that your love?

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:21.460
It is.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:40.810
He's just late. He <i>will</i> come back.

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:46.280
He'll announce himself and kiss
my hand without a hint of shame.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:48.200
I know he will.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:50.870
Richard.

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:55.200
Can you hear them, Richard?

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.790
I know you can hear those longing cries.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:01.130
They call the name of a king.

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:03.800
Now go, Richard.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.930
I am with you.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:08.840
King Richard!

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.050
It's King Richard!

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:12.350
King Richard III is here!

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:19.230
Noble and bold people of York.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:22.310
Thank you for your warm welcome.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:26.240
I once beheld hell in this city.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:30.860
The sun was extinguished,
leaving only deepest darkness.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:35.490
Such was the death of my father,
whom I loved him best in all the world.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:38.500
Yet for all the tears I shed on his grave,

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:42.960
my sword shed far more enemy
blood on the field of battle!

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:46.670
And now,

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:49.760
I have returned here!

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:55.010
I offer this golden light to my
great father and the city of York!

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:56.850
King Richard III!

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:58.810
Long live the king!

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.780
Light for this city.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:17.450
I wish to promote those whom
the light has not yet touched.

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:18.750
Once I return to London--

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:19.750
Your Majesty!

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:22.880
A man just delivered this.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:27.380
This is from Buckingham!

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:28.590
And the messenger?

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:34.180
His, um, hood hid his face,
but he bid me give you this.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:35.300
It can't be!

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.850
Richard?

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:42.600
I know that you'll come back.
I'm certain of it!

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:44.810
You will

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:46.230
return to me!

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:49.570
Henry!

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:02.000
It can't be.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:06.750
Who is he? Am I hallucinating?

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:10.880
You're wrong, Richard. I'm James Tyrrell.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:13.050
Your assassin.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.020
It's not time for that yet.

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:29.320
This man is James Tyrrell?

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:33.400
He's the very image of Henry VI.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:34.740
How...?

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.410
How could this be?

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:38.660
Even his voice is identical.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:42.580
I need to know you better.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.420
Before the time comes.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:48.040
--Wait!
--Your Majesty!

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:51.550
You were late in returning.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:53.800
Did the Duke of Buckingham...?

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.720
It wasn't him.

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:02.100
It wasn't Henry.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:12.110
That clown gave us these sweets.

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:15.070
I'll eat them all while Edward's sleeping.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:16.110
Damnation!

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:17.610
E-Edward?

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:20.240
Damn! Damn! Damn!
I'm too furious to sleep!

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:22.790
Why don't my "supporters"
come to my rescue?!

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:24.120
Are they all incompetent?!

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:26.330
P-Please calm down, Edward.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:33.170
Try to imagine something happy,
like what you'll do once you're restored.

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:34.210
Good idea.

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:38.760
If he ever does get the throne back,

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:42.060
I'll have to go back to waiting
on him like a servant.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:47.020
Before that happens,
I might as well just...

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:48.270
I'll start with a feast.

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:49.690
Huh?

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:53.400
I'll summon Mother, and Elizabeth, too.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.530
And then

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:58.660
I'll execute Richard as
an example to everyone.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:02.620
And his son too?

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.950
After we show him his
father's miserable corpse.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:08.710
How his wife will weep and despair!

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:11.790
We'll bake the bodies into pies
and make his servants eat them.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:13.840
We'll toast with blood for wine!

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.840
Why stop there?
Let's think up something crueler.

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:20.760
I feel a bit better.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.430
Huh?

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:26.020
If you weren't here...

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:29.810
If I were alone, I would have gone mad.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:32.610
S-Stop. That's not like you.

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:37.110
Will we kill each other someday too?

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:41.700
Like our father and our uncles did?

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.950
I've been thinking.

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:47.330
If we get out of here...

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:52.290
...I'd like us to be friends.

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:54.590
Edward.

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:01.680
Shall we eat them together?

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.350
Hey. Keep quiet.

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:10.980
What does it matter?
Our client owns the Tower.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.780
How sweet they look.

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:20.820
This must be the beauty
of the Lord's chosen.

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:24.410
Still, they sleep like logs.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:27.120
Almost like they're dead already.

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:29.250
Hm?

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:36.750
One can never be too careful.
Hard biscuits are best for long journeys.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:44.350
Henry.

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:45.350
Richard.

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:46.430
Not you!

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:49.810
I need to know you better.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:51.520
What the devil does it mean?!

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:53.600
I feel like I'm losing my mind.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:57.820
What is there to fear?

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:02.070
<i>We</i> are God's anointed king.

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:05.120
That's right. The war is over.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:07.530
No one can threaten me now.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.160
Pardon me.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.170
Tidings just arrived from London.

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:16.840
Your Majesty?

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:23.680
Buckingham is... in revolt.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:30.180
The Duke of Buckingham, revolt?

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:31.350
Impossible.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:34.140
Richard.

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:39.940
Unless you relinquish your crown in
one month's time, by St. Luke's Day,

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:44.820
an army will march on London
to dethrone Richard III.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:49.950
Therefore, I cannot go to York.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:53.250
I have only one wish.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:59.630
Richard, a forest called Dean
lies on the road to my castle.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:03.800
Let us meet there. We will cross
the river, and then the sea.

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:06.470
Richard...

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:15.520
Forsake your crown and come to
those woods before the day appointed.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:18.020
Your Majesty.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:19.110
Your Majesty!

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:23.030
Say nothing of this to anyone.

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:26.610
Which matter do you mean?

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.700
Buckingham, of course!

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:31.740
I beg your pardon.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:35.120
Forgive me, Catesby.

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:38.830
Now, what news from London?

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:41.800
The children in the Tower are gone.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.260
Make haste to London.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:44.090
Certainly.

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.260
No, wait!

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:50.140
Something's wrong.
If the rebels absconded with them,

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:52.310
could Buckingham be involved?

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:57.190
To quash the rebellion, I must raise
troops and strike the foe before--

00:13:57.190 --> 00:14:00.110
Foe? Am I going to slay him?

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:01.230
Nonsense!

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:08.950
Spread rumors that the children are dead.
They'll make poor figureheads that way.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.530
At once.

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:13.080
Why, Henry?

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.080
Why?!

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:52.120
It can't be.

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:55.490
Would that it were but a nightmare.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:59.000
Yet there are witnesses.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:03.340
The lifeless bodies of King
Edward V and Prince Richard

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:07.510
were taken from the Tower
in the dead of night.

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:11.140
How horrible!

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:15.010
No! No! Not my darling sons!

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:16.890
No. It isn't true.

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:18.600
Why, God?!

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:24.110
That beautiful sapling should have grown
to prop up all of England as king!

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:26.940
And yet... And yet...

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:29.990
That demon must have done it!

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:34.160
How much will you take from me
before you're satisfied, Richard?!

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:36.700
Why not kill me as well?!

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:38.410
Make Westminster my grave, and--

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:43.420
Your Majesty mustn't say such things.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:49.010
Look. You still have a fine princess.

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:55.050
You're right. The Lord sends us trials,

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:59.220
but justice always wins out in the end.

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:02.690
We shall unite our two lights

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:06.320
and help them ascend to a lofty
height second only to God.

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:10.440
My Beth and your son Richmond

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:14.070
will reach England's
highest rank of dignity.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:19.040
How odd. The brothers always
look out of that window.

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:22.040
Now that you mention it,
I haven't seen them.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:25.580
They've vanished from the Tower.
Rumor has it they're dead.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:28.050
How could it be a mystery?

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:30.920
They were in the palace.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:32.970
Our greatest enemy is within.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:35.680
He'll never let anyone
stand in his way and live.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:39.930
He even slew innocent children
to defend his stolen throne!

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:42.350
Tear that demon from the throne!

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.730
Soldiers swarm to join us.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.980
The stratagem was a success.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:51.440
The Marquess of Dorset,
who was in hiding, sends word

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:56.280
that the boys' death has
sparked uprisings far and wide.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:58.200
What of Richmond?

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:01.200
He sailed from Brittany leading troops,

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:06.630
and his mother has obtained Queen
Elizabeth's consent to that matter.

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:08.170
And Stanley?

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:11.340
Naturally, he'll join his wife and son.

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:13.970
He <i>is</i> our intermediary.

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:18.260
My father was a Lancastrian.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:20.930
And so you follow suit!

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:25.770
My blood and title are both
worthless to me now.

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:28.730
I want only one thing.

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:31.820
Only you, Richard.

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:34.150
Your Majesty honors me!

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:38.700
Lend me your strength
to build a new England.

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:43.040
Nothing would give us
northerners more pleasure.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:48.210
I pledge that my soul shall
always be with Your Majesty.

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:50.630
Do I go to the forest where he waits,

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:53.920
or do I face down rebellion as a king?

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.800
The appointed day is almost upon us.

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:57.930
Hey, everybody!

00:17:57.930 --> 00:18:00.100
His Majesty was just here!

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:02.810
Our king!

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:05.390
Must I choose?

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:10.060
You must know better than
anyone how I longed for that.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.820
Mother?

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:13.190
What's wrong?!

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:20.700
Perhaps I've overexerted myself.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:23.620
It's my turn to fall ill.

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:26.500
I've burdened you.

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:29.580
Because of my indecision...

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:31.750
It's not your fault.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:35.800
In fact, I feel better in York.

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:40.220
Part of me always wondered

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:43.060
if choosing you was a mistake.

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:50.020
Was it right for you to become
king and for me to support you?

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:53.860
But when I saw the people bless you,

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:57.240
it struck me that this is a new beginning.

00:18:57.240 --> 00:19:03.240
When you spoke of England's future,
you looked like your father in profile.

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:06.620
You were noble and beautiful.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:07.540
Anne.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:11.080
I'll get well soon.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.670
Edward will have his
knighting ceremony soon.

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:20.470
Edward, rise as a knight.

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:26.470
Be a guardian to all
the just and the weak.

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:28.480
Yes, Your Majesty!

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.230
Father!

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:43.990
Are you well?

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:50.290
I don't want that boy's childhood
to be sorrowful, like ours was.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:54.170
Let's make a land for him, together.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:57.130
A beautiful kingdom.

00:19:57.130 --> 00:20:01.340
Amid betrayal after betrayal,
they chose me.

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:04.300
Both Anne and Buckingham.

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:07.310
I can't lose one of them.

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:08.890
I can't make that choice.

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:11.810
Your Majesty.

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:13.350
Catesby.

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:15.560
What's my schedule today?

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:17.690
Inspecting an abbey?

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:20.030
Your Majesty! King Richard!

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:25.570
Command me. The day is nearly here.

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:27.990
Will you gather troops?

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:29.620
Or go to the forest?

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.550
You think I could?

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:43.880
What would become of Anne
and Edward with me gone?

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:46.010
What of the people who believed in me?

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:52.430
I merely obey your wishes.

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:54.350
My wishes?

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:00.440
I'll...

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:05.200
I'll speak to Buckingham once more!

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:07.780
That's right. There are other ways.

00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:09.910
No one yet knows of his rebellion.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:11.500
There's still hope for--

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:12.500
Your Majesty!

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:16.750
Urgent news! Kent is in revolt!

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:20.840
Our forces in Kent have risen?

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.300
I gave no order!

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:25.550
The king must know our plans now.

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:28.510
It's a little premature,
but we must march.

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:32.520
Come, Your Grace, signal the advance!

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:34.850
What's so shocking about that?

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:37.060
Kent is always rebellious.

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:39.270
His Grace, the Duke of
Buckingham is behind it!

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:40.860
This is treason!

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:42.990
Yes! He's turned on us!

00:21:42.990 --> 00:21:44.490
Your Majesty! Your orders?!

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:45.820
We must act at once!
